      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Purpose:\n- Transfer body pose and stance.\n\nInputs:\n- Image 1 = target person.\n- Image 2 = pose reference.\n\nStarter prompt idea:\n- \"Make the person in Image 1 adopt the exact pose and body angle seen in Image 2. Preserve the face identity and clothing details of Image 1.\"\n\nRecommended advanced upgrade:\n- Install ComfyUI-ControlNetAux (for DWPose / OpenPose preprocessing).\n- Install ComfyUI-Impact-Pack if you want FaceDetailer for better face recovery.\n\nRuntime notes:\n- This starter file works immediately with semantic pose transfer.\n- After installing the advanced nodes, you can evolve it into a more explicit DWPose-guided setup.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n    Identity Preservation Rules:\n    - The main person's face identity must stay stable.\n    - Keep face shape, eye spacing, nose shape, mouth shape, skin characteristics, and recognizable appearance.\n    - If multiple reference images are used, they may influence clothing, pose, lighting, background, or materials — not identity, unless explicitly designated as the identity reference.\n    - For edits that do not require face changes, prefer keeping the face untouched or minimally changed.\n    - If identity drift happens in practice, recommended recovery stack:\n      1) make Image 1 the identity anchor,\n      2) keep the prompt explicit about preserving identity,\n      3) use local/cropped editing for non-face changes,\n      4) use ReActor as a final face restore/fallback pass,\n      5) optionally use FaceDetailer with low denoise for face cleanup only.\n    - In this workflow, Image 1 is the identity anchor.\n- Image 2 is pose-only reference; it must not replace the person's identity.\n- For stronger identity retention, consider adding ReActor as a final face restore stage.\n\nPrompt Guard Upgrade:\n- The positive prompt is now split into:\n  1) SYSTEM PROMPT — protected identity-preserving rules\n  2) USER PROMPT — the part you edit\n- The negative prompt is also split into:\n  1) SYSTEM NEGATIVE — protected anti-drift / anti-face-mismatch rules\n  2) USER NEGATIVE — optional extra negatives\n- This prevents accidental deletion of the identity-preservation logic during normal use."
      ],
      "title": "03 — Pose Transfer Pro — Guide & Prompt",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
